<h3 id="kraus">My Creations</h3>

<p>My first steps as an entrepreneur were in the consulting field, focusing on technologies such as Adobe Flash Media Server and Adobe Flex. I traveled across Brazil teaching courses and enthusiastically sharing my knowledge. This initial phase provided me with a solid foundation for what was to come.</p>

<p>It was during this time that the opportunity arose to create Kopere Meeting, a platform similar to Google Meet, but with an important distinction: support for end-to-end encryption. At that time, Adobe Connect was an expensive option, and companies were looking for alternatives that offered absolute confidentiality in communications between their branches. Kopere Meeting filled that gap, resulting in many valuable contracts with companies that valued the privacy of their conversations.</p>

<p>In addition, I constantly sought innovation and the development of new tools. A notable example was the creation of WebTV, a high-definition video streaming environment. This platform was developed using advanced technologies such as Adobe Flex and object-oriented PHP, with essential support from the Wowza server. WebTV enabled the broadcasting of lectures and events in high definition over the internet, meeting the growing demand for high-quality audiovisual content.</p>

<p>The decision to start my own company was, therefore, a natural response to the unique combination of experiences and knowledge I had accumulated over time. Each stage of my journey contributed to my growth as an entrepreneur, enabling me to identify opportunities and offer innovative solutions in the ever-evolving world of technology and business.</p>

